menuconfig CTLV
	tristate "CTLV character device TLV UAPI framework"
	# A blob attr may name a dma-buf, whatever family declares one.
	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
	help
	  CTLV is a framework for character device UAPIs that are described by
	  a checked-in YAML specification instead of hand-written wire
	  definitions. It owns the character device lifetime, the strict TLV
	  message format, request validation, reply serialization, the large
	  payloads a request describes rather than carries, per-open event
	  queues and runtime schema introspection, so that families and their
	  drivers only implement semantics.

	  If you don't know what to do here, say N.
